            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "57suze"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The vinegar was overpowering in this during the cooking phase and I was concerned it was going to ruin the salmon I was preparing, but was surprised at how good it was on the fish. I did not have apricots and I used agave instead of sugar."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "der golem"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Spectacular idea, a great balance of sweet, tart, tangy. \n\nI admit that I improvised a lot. But that's what makes this a great recipe. \n\nI had a couple of over ripe apricots and some mango. Grated in some ginger. A bit of water, some white balsamic vinegar substituted for the rice vinegar/sugar reduction. A squeeze of lime to finish. I can use it on chicken, but also shrimp or even drizzle on an english muffin, over plain yogurt, pancakes.",
            "datePublished": "2020-06-08T23:29:43.573Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kateri"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've rated this a four but in fairness I didn't follow the recipe, I used it as a guideline. I was putting this on ham and one of my family isn't a fan of apricots. I substituted brown sugar for the white sugar, I didn't have fresh ginger, so used ground ginger instead - next time it will be fresh. With using brown sugar the amount of rice vinegar was fine. I also added a little bit of crushed red chili pepper.",
            "datePublished": "2018-05-05T02:29:55.443Z"
          }
        ],
